.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "fast-levenshtein - Levenshtein algorithm in Javascript"
.PP
\fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP

.PP
An efficient Javascript implementation of the \fRLevenshtein algorithm\fP with locale-specific collator support\&.
.SH "Features"
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Works in node\&.js and in the browser\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Better performance than other implementations by not needing to store the whole matrix (\fRmore info\fP)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Locale-sensitive string comparisions if needed\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Comprehensive test suite and performance benchmark\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Small: <1 KB minified and gzipped
.PP
.SH "Installation"
.PP
.SS "node\&.js"
Install using [npm](http://npmjs.org/):

.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm install fast\-levenshtein
.fi
.PP
.SS "Browser"
Using bower:

.PP
.PP
.nf
$ bower install fast\-levenshtein
.fi
.PP

.PP
If you are not using any module loader system then the API will then be accessible via the `window\&.Levenshtein` object\&.
.SH "Examples"
.PP
**Default usage**

.PP
.PP
.nf
var levenshtein = require('fast\-levenshtein');

var distance = levenshtein\&.get('back', 'book');   // 2
var distance = levenshtein\&.get('我愛你', '我叫你');   // 1
.fi
.PP

.PP
**Locale-sensitive string comparisons**

.PP
It supports using [Intl\&.Collator](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Collator) for locale-sensitive string comparisons:

.PP
.PP
.nf
var levenshtein = require('fast\-levenshtein');

levenshtein\&.get('mikailovitch', 'Mikhaïlovitch', { useCollator: true});
// 1
.fi
.PP
.SH "Building and Testing"
.PP
To build the code and run the tests:

.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm install \-g grunt\-cli
$ npm install
$ npm run build
.fi
.PP
.SH "Performance"
.PP
_Thanks to [Titus Wormer](https://github.com/wooorm) for [encouraging me](https://github.com/hiddentao/fast-levenshtein/issues/1) to do this\&._

.PP
Benchmarked against other node\&.js levenshtein distance modules (on Macbook Air 2012, Core i7, 8GB RAM):

.PP
.PP
.nf
Running suite Implementation comparison [benchmark/speed\&.js]\&.\&.\&.
>> levenshtein\-edit\-distance x 234 ops/sec ±3\&.02% (73 runs sampled)
>> levenshtein\-component x 422 ops/sec ±4\&.38% (83 runs sampled)
>> levenshtein\-deltas x 283 ops/sec ±3\&.83% (78 runs sampled)
>> natural x 255 ops/sec ±0\&.76% (88 runs sampled)
>> levenshtein x 180 ops/sec ±3\&.55% (86 runs sampled)
>> fast\-levenshtein x 1,792 ops/sec ±2\&.72% (95 runs sampled)
Benchmark done\&.
Fastest test is fast\-levenshtein at 4\&.2x faster than levenshtein\-component
.fi
.PP

.PP
You can run this benchmark yourself by doing:

.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm install
$ npm run build
$ npm run benchmark
.fi
.PP
